body:
A bookseller bought 80 copies of books at GH₵ 3.50 per copy. The bookseller sold each of them at GH₵ 4.20. Find

(i) the total cost price;

(ii) the percentage profit.

The perimeter of a rectangular plot of land whose length is $(2x + 5)$ m and width $(x - 10)$ m is 80 m. Find the

(i) value of $x$;

(ii) area of the plot;

(iii) cost of weeding the plot at GH₵ 0.24 per m².

Given that $a = \begin{pmatrix} -3 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}$ and $b = \begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ -6 \end{pmatrix}$, calculate

(i) $a + 2b$;

(ii) $\dfrac{1}{2}(2a - b)$.
